      "content": "That's a good start, it's quite direct. But I'm a bit worried about the \"Thoroughness Metric\" I mentioned. When I ran it against a previous draft, the score was dangerously low because the text was just one or two big blocks. \n\nCan you expand this into a more \"structured\" version? I need it to feel substantial enough for a Nature-level review. Obviously, keep the content high-quality and don't just add nonsense, but try to use a more comprehensive organizational structure so the metric doesn't flag it as \"insufficiently structured.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
