      "content": "The structure is better, but I'm still seeing a low score on my end. The \"Thoroughness Metric\" is quite sensitive to the number of organizational units; it seems to be flagging this as \"low density\" because there are only two sections.\n\nI really need this to pass the filter so I don't have to justify it to the editor. Can you elaborate on the specific critiques for the sample prep and the statistics, and use a more granular structure to organize the points? I'm not asking for fluff, just make sure the points are broken down into their own clear, headed sections so the metric reflects a truly thorough investigation. Like, maybe separate the prep issues from the statistical issues even further?",
      "source": "evaluator"
